## Typing stubs for unidiff

This is a [type stub package](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/tutorials/external_libraries.html)
for the [`unidiff`](https://github.com/matiasb/python-unidiff) package. It can be used by type checkers
to check code that uses `unidiff`. This version of
`types-unidiff` aims to provide accurate annotations for
`unidiff==0.7.*`.

*Note:* The `unidiff` package includes type annotations or type stubs
since version 1.0.0. Please uninstall the `types-unidiff`
package if you use this or a newer version.


This package is part of the [typeshed project](https://github.com/python/typeshed).
All fixes for types and metadata should be contributed there.
See [the README](https://github.com/python/typeshed/blob/main/README.md)
for more details. The source for this package can be found in the
[`stubs/unidiff`](https://github.com/python/typeshed/tree/main/stubs/unidiff)
directory.

This package was tested with the following type checkers:
* [mypy](https://github.com/python/mypy/) 2.3.0
* [pyright](https://github.com/microsoft/pyright) 1.1.411

It was generated from typeshed commit
[`41308b88d4dc51e8d165a8839c2f0f12bdf43173`](https://github.com/python/typeshed/commit/41308b88d4dc51e8d165a8839c2f0f12bdf43173).
